WEBVTT
Kind: subtitles
Language: en

1
00:00.290 --> 00:02.820
So what is the hypothesis-led approach to problem solving?

2
00:03.210 --> 00:08.400
Well, by definition, it's asking you to have a hypothesis.
And it's taking a very structured approach

3
00:08.400 --> 00:18.140
and asking you, when you define the problem upfront, to think about what is the hypothesis
you're trying to prove or disprove — and make some assertions about that.

4
00:18.210 --> 00:26.400
Then, as you think about the prioritization and the structuring of the work,
it's around how you test those hypotheses to get to a better answer more quickly.

5
00:26.400 --> 00:33.080
It's also an approach that is widely applicable
to a range of problems. It scales quite nicely.

6
00:33.160 --> 00:38.400
And it doesn't assume a tremendous amount of expertise,
so a lot of folks can use it.

7
00:38.400 --> 00:47.450
So let's think about an example of where the hypothesis-led approach may apply. If you're thinking
about making a big investment — perhaps even acquiring another company — that's a pretty broad question.

8
00:47.780 --> 00:54.200
You may not have a tremendous amount of expertise, and you may not have access to a ton of data.
But it's a question with a very clear answer.

9
00:54.200 --> 01:02.650
You either will invest or you won't invest.
You will acquire the company or you won't acquire the company.

10
01:02.790 --> 01:08.400
And so, in that sense, being able to take that fundamental question
as your starting point — should you do this? —

11
01:08.400 --> 01:13.600
and then think about how you structure that problem
and break it down into the component parts:

12
01:13.600 --> 01:19.070
those are great examples of where the hypothesis-led approach can be really powerful.
What makes me really excited about the hypothesis-led approach

13
01:19.140 --> 01:25.400
is that it provides a great structure to enable me
to be a more creative problem solver.

14
01:25.400 --> 01:33.050
And so there's both the art and the science in terms of problem solving.
And the science in the hypothesis-led approach is around

15
01:33.290 --> 01:40.350
thinking through, in a very structured way, how you take
a very large, complex, ambiguous, hard-to-define problem,

16
01:40.680 --> 01:46.200
break it down into the component parts,
and ultimately get to an actionable recommendation.

17
01:46.200 --> 01:56.570
The art in the process is really the creative element. And what I love is that creative tension
when you're debating how we really define the problem — is one version of the issue tree superior to another?

18
01:56.650 --> 02:06.270
The hypothesis-led approach creates that structure to really enable
those creative collaborations — and that is really the power of the approach.
